INT. GONDOLA CABLE CAR - ALPINE PASS - NIGHT

A steel box the size of a closet, swaying one degree at a time. Frost climbs the windows. Far below, the resort lights blink on a timer nobody can reach.

OKSANA VOLK (60s, retired nurse, wool hat pulled to her eyebrows) breaks a chocolate bar into six squares with her thumbnail. She hands them out in order of age, oldest to youngest.

TEODOR (30s, lift mechanic, grease in the creases of his knuckles) turns the dial on a radio. Static. He turns it back. Static.

ARJUN (17, rental skis between his knees) checks his phone. No bars. He checks it again.

MIREILLE (40s, immaculate parka, one glove missing) tucks her bare hand into her armpit and says nothing about it.

BRAM (50s, broad, red-faced) holds his square of chocolate without eating it.

PIP (8) licks hers slowly, making it last.

TEODOR
Wind drops by morning. They send the snowcat.

OKSANA
Good.

BRAM passes his chocolate to Pip. Pip looks at Oksana. Oksana nods once. Pip takes it.

MIREILLE slides her glove off the other hand and gives it to Arjun without looking at him. He puts it on.

The car sways. Nobody mentions it.
